            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 21-year-old female patient, admitted on 03/12/2020 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection. On admission, she presented with fever, dry cough, and dyspnoea. A chest X-ray confirmed bilateral infiltrates consistent with COVID-19 pneumonia. Blood tests and arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia. Pulse oximetry monitoring was performed continuously throughout her stay. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, antiviral medication, and supportive intravenous fluids. Physical examination was conducted daily, and vital signs were closely monitored. The patient responded well to treatment, with gradual clinical improvement. She was discharged on 05/12/2020 in a recovering condition with instructions for home isolation and follow-up. Patient education regarding infection control and symptom monitoring was provided prior to discharge. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
